{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DAnGzkF4tpXJUDYhdNy9GV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the task and plan my approach before writing code.\n\n**Task**: Create unit tests for the differential testing harness in `pkg/testutils/`. Two files need to be created:\n1. `pkg/testutils/runner_test.go` - Tests for `buildEnv`, `setEnvVar`, `formatDivergence`, `truncateBytes`, `compareExpectedFiles`\n2. `pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go` - Tests for `TimestampNormalizer`, `ComposeNormalizers`, `applyNormalizers`\n\n**Required Reading**: I need to read `prd001-testutils.yaml` for requirements R2-R5. The source code is already provided inline.\n\n\nNow I'm mapping out the test cases I need to write. For `runner_test.go`, I'll verify that `buildEnv` correctly sets LC_ALL=C and merges caller-provided variables without duplication, test `setEnvVar` for both new and override scenarios, check that `formatDivergence` includes all the expected output fields like arguments, stdin, and exit codes, and validate the truncation and file comparison functions. For `difftest_test.go`, I need to test the normalizer implementations and how they compose together. I'm looking at the PR description to understand the context and scope of these test cases.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24454,"cache_read_input_tokens":16066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24454},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b30a63d-c030-4034-a5d1-c65c1813eda0","uuid":"0fdb59e6-023e-422e-b3c7-232c632bf7b2"}
